# **Required review is deliberately off, and turning it on locks `main`.**
# GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request, so requiring one
# from a single code owner leaves no one who can approve anything: a gate that
# exists only by being bypassed. It was set once and did exactly that.
#
# On the day there is a second person: required approvals to 1,
# `require_code_owner_reviews` on, and this file names a team instead.
#
# The `main` ruleset requires the `verify` context, which is a *job* name and
# not a workflow name. `verify.yml` shards into `checks (0..9)`, four `browser`
# entries and the rest; `verify` is the aggregation job that needs them all, so
# the required check survives the shard count changing under it.

